# Strip speaker notes from QMD files before committing.
# Notes remain in working directory but never enter git history.
# Setup: ./scripts/setup-git-filters.sh (run once after clone)
#
# The pattern must stay recursive. A gitattributes pattern containing a slash
# is anchored, and `*` does not cross a directory separator -- so `Quarto/*.qmd`
# silently stops matching the moment a deck lives in Quarto/papers/ or
# Quarto/lectures/. Nothing fails and nothing warns; the notes just land in git.
# `scripts/test_note_filter.sh` asserts this stays true.
Quarto/**/*.qmd filter=strip-speaker-notes
